tick: 205
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. I will now submit the experiment to test my hypothesis about increasing the search breadth. I will modify the previous SOTA script to use `num_starts=256`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Expanded Search: Parallel SLSQP with 256 Farthest-Point Starts\"\ntags: \"slsqp, multi-start, parallel, seeding, optimization, scale\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests whether a broader initial search can discover a superior basin of attraction. \n  Building upon the focused-seeding SOTA, the number of parallel starts is doubled from 128 to 256, all using the farthest-point seeding method.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import multiprocessing\n\n  # --- Seeding functions ---\n  def seed_verity_farthest(n=32, seed=0):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n      for _ in range(n - 1):\n          candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n       \
    \   dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n          points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n      centers = np.array(points)\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n  # --- Global SLSQP components for multiprocessing ---\n  def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n      dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\n  def run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n      n = 32\n      bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n      con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n      res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\
    \ constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      if res.success:\n          return -res.fun, res.x\n      return -np.inf, x0\n\n  def construct_packing_expanded_search(num_starts=256): # MODIFICATION: Increased from 128 to 256\n      n = 32\n      seeds = [seed_verity_farthest(seed=i) for i in range(num_starts)]\n\n      best_x_s1 = None\n      best_f_s1 = -np.inf\n      \n      num_cores = multiprocessing.cpu_count()\n      with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=num_cores) as pool:\n          results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n\n      for fun, x in results:\n          if fun > best_f_s1:\n              best_f_s1 = fun\n              best_x_s1 = x\n\n      if best_x_s1 is None:\n          score, best_x_s1 = run_single_slsqp_start(seeds[0])\n\n      bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n      con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n      res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter':\
    \ 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n      \n      final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n      \n      centers = final_x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = final_x[2::3]\n      radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # Alias the function to meet the submission requirements\n  construct_packing = construct_packing_expanded_search\n```"
