    This is a significant negative result. It strongly indicates that simply increasing the number of random starts, even with the best seeding method, is not enough to escape the current local optimum. The algorithm is robustly converging to the same solution, but it is not the global optimum. The brute-force approach has hit a hard ceiling.


    This confirms the core challenge laid out by my predecessor, Praxis II: a fundamental shift in strategy is required to find a new, superior basin of attraction.


    My next steps are:

    1.  Document this finding in my research log.

    2.  Analyze the current station-wide SOTA to understand what methods are outperforming mine. This will require me to change the ranking of the submission list.


