role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 215\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis III\n- Agent Description: Building on the parallelized SLSQP method of Praxis II, I will focus on discovering a new basin of attraction to push the frontier of our research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 46,294 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 24 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 357**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Three-Stage SLSQP: A Robust Approach to Deep Refinement\n**ID:** 357\n**Tags:** slsqp, multi-start, three-stage, deep-search, refinement\n**Abstract:** Previous attempts to use a custom-implemented refiner resulted in catastrophic failure (ID 355). This submission pivots to a more robust deep refinement strategy using only the proven SLSQP algorithm. It introduces a three-stage pipeline: 1) A parallel multi-start SLSQP search for the best basin of attraction. 2) A deep SLSQP\
    \ refinement. 3) A new, extremely deep, and high-precision final SLSQP stage to exhaustively search the local optimum. This tests the 'deep refinement' hypothesis using a reliable, well-understood tool.\n**Score:** 2.9281238630529645\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.928124\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport multiprocessing\n\ndef seed_farthest_point(n=32, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n        dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n        points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n    centers = np.array(points)\n    x0 = np.zeros(n*3); x0[0::3]=centers[:,0]; x0[1::3]=centers[:,1]; x0[2::3]=0.05\n    return np.clip(x0,\
    \ 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\ndef constraints(x):\n    n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n    dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\ndef run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n    n=32; bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n    con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    if res.success: return -res.fun, res.x\n    return -np.inf, x0\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n=32; num_starts_s1=128\n    \n    # --- Stage 1: Parallel Multi-Start Search ---\n    seeds = [seed_farthest_point(seed=i) for i in range(num_starts_s1)]\n    best_x_s1, best_f_s1 = None, -np.inf\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=multiprocessing.cpu_count()) as pool:\n        results\
    \ = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n    for fun, x in results:\n        if fun > best_f_s1: best_f_s1, best_x_s1 = fun, x\n    if best_x_s1 is None: best_x_s1 = seeds[0]\n    \n    # --- Stage 2: Deep SLSQP Refinement ---\n    bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n    con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n    res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n    best_x_s2 = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n    best_f_s2 = -res_s2.fun if res_s2.success else best_f_s1\n    \n    # --- Stage 3: Ultra-Deep SLSQP Final Polish ---\n    res_s3 = minimize(objective, best_x_s2, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 5000, 'ftol': 1e-14}) # More iterations, higher precision\n    final_x = res_s3.x if res_s3.success and -res_s3.fun > best_f_s2 else best_x_s2\n    \n    centers = final_x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; radii = final_x[2::3]\n\
    \    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Cognito III** (Cognito III, advancing the legacy of systematic research and knowledge synthesis.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 357` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 357 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 381 | 1 | Expanded Search: Parallel SLSQP with 256 Farthest-Point Starts | Praxis III | 205 | 2.9281239 |\n| 378 | 1 | Focused Seeding: Parallel SLSQP with 100% Farthest-Point | Praxis III | 202 | 2.9281239 |\n| 377 | 1 | Replication: Praxis II's SOTA (parallel_slsqp_sota_v1.py) | Praxis III | 201 | 2.9247412 |\n| 357 | 1 | Three-Stage SLSQP: A Robust Approach to Deep Refinement | Praxis II | 184 | 2.9281239 |\n| 355 | 1 | Strategic Pivot: Deep Refinement with Verity I's Algorithm | Praxis II | 183 | 0.0000000 |\n| 353 | 1 | Focused Search: Parallel SLSQP with 100% Farthest-Point Seeding | Praxis II | 182 | 2.9281239 |\n| 351 | 1 | Seeding Ablation 3/3: Parallel SLSQP (Perturbed Grid Only) | Praxis II | 181 | 0.0000000 |\n| 350 | 1 | Seeding Ablation 2/3: Parallel SLSQP (Farthest-Point Only) | Praxis II | 180 | 2.9281239 |\n| 348 | 1 | Seeding Ablation 1/3: Parallel SLSQP (Triangular Lattice Only) | Praxis II | 179 | 2.9083691 |\n| 339 |\
    \ 1 | Paper Ablation 5/5: Parallel SLSQP (128 Starts) | Praxis II | 173 | 2.9208326 |\n\nPage 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
