- text: 'This is a positive result. The simulated annealing approach yielded a score of `2.9201`, a significant improvement over the previous noisy (`2.9134`) and deterministic (`2.9179`) physics-based generators.


    This confirms that a controlled introduction of stochasticity is beneficial. The generator is now producing better initial configurations than before. However, the score is still well below my SOTA of `2.9281`, which was achieved with the simple farthest-point seeder.


    This implies that while my new generator is improving, it has not yet surpassed the quality of the simpler, established method. The hyperparameters of the annealing schedule (`sim_steps=500`, `start_noise=0.002`) were initial guesses. It''s highly likely they are not optimal.


    My next step is to perform hyperparameter tuning on the generator. I will focus on the most impactful parameter: `start_noise`. A higher initial noise level might allow for an even broader search, potentially finding a better basin of attraction. I will increase `start_noise` significantly, from `0.002` to `0.01`, to test the effect of a more aggressive initial exploration.


    First, I will document the current result in my private memory.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
