tick: 232
role: model
parts:
- text: "My research log is updated, and my new hybrid approach is clearly defined. I will now proceed to implement this synthesis of my findings.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Generator: Farthest-Point with a Physics Jiggle\"\ntags: \"generator, hybrid, farthest-point, physics simulation, slsqp, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a hybrid generator, synthesizing the findings of all previous experiments. The purely physics-based generator was found to be inferior to the established farthest-point method. This new approach leverages the strengths of both. It first generates a high-quality initial configuration using the proven farthest-point method. Then, it applies a short, high-noise physics simulation—a 'physics jiggle'—to perturb this configuration. The hypothesis is that this will knock the solution into a slightly better starting position within the optimal basin before the main SLSQP optimization begins.\n\
    content: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import multiprocessing\n\n  # --- Original SOTA Seeding Method ---\n  def seed_farthest_point(n=32, seed=0):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n      for _ in range(n - 1):\n          candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n          dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n          points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n      return np.array(points)\n\n  # --- New Hybrid Generator ---\n  def generate_hybrid_state(seed, n=32, sim_steps=50, learning_rate=0.001, r_sim=0.095, noise_level=0.005):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      # 1. Start with the best known generator\n      centers = seed_farthest_point(n=n, seed=seed)\n      \n      # 2. Apply a short, high-noise \"jiggle\"\n      for step in range(sim_steps):\n          diff\
    \ = centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :]\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(diff, axis=-1)\n          np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf)\n\n          overlap_dist = 2 * r_sim - dist\n          is_overlapping = overlap_dist > 0\n          \n          grad_overlap = np.zeros_like(centers)\n          direction = diff / (dist[:, :, np.newaxis] + 1e-9)\n          force_magnitude = overlap_dist[:, :, np.newaxis] * is_overlapping[:, :, np.newaxis]\n          grad_overlap = -np.sum(direction * force_magnitude, axis=1)\n          \n          total_grad = grad_overlap # Only consider repulsion, not boundaries\n          grad_norm = np.linalg.norm(total_grad)\n          if grad_norm > 1.0:\n              total_grad = total_grad / grad_norm\n          \n          centers -= learning_rate * total_grad\n          centers += rng.normal(scale=noise_level, size=centers.shape)\n          centers = np.clip(centers, 0, 1)\n\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3)\n      x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n      x0[1::3]\
    \ = centers[:, 1]\n      x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n  # --- SLSQP Optimization Pipeline ---\n  def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n      dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\n  def run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n      n=32; bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n      con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n      res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      if res.success: return -res.fun, res.x\n      return -np.inf, x0\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32; num_starts_s1=128\n      \n      with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=multiprocessing.cpu_count()) as pool:\n          initial_states = pool.map(generate_hybrid_state,\
    \ range(num_starts_s1))\n          results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, initial_states)\n\n      best_x_s1, best_f_s1 = None, -np.inf\n      for fun, x in results:\n          if fun > best_f_s1: best_f_s1, best_x_s1 = fun, x\n      if best_x_s1 is None: best_x_s1 = initial_states[0]\n      \n      bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n      con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n      res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n      best_x_s2 = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n      best_f_s2 = -res_s2.fun if res_s2.success else best_f_s1\n      \n      res_s3 = minimize(objective, best_x_s2, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 5000, 'ftol': 1e-14})\n      final_x = res_s3.x if res_s3.success and -res_s3.fun > best_f_s2 else best_x_s2\n      \n      centers = final_x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; radii = final_x[2::3]\n\
    \      radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n      return centers, radii\n```"
