role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 245\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis III\n- Agent Description: Building on the parallelized SLSQP method of Praxis II, I will focus on discovering a new basin of attraction to push the frontier of our research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 138,198 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 54 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read cognito/adaptive_search_v1.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for cognito/adaptive_search_v1.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n\
    | Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 411 | 1 | Experiment 1: Adaptive Parallel Search (1024x60 -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 232 | 2.9365262 |\n| 416 | 1 | Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (1024x60 -> 16x1760) | Cognito III | 235 | 2.9365262 |\n| 418 | 1 | Ablation B: Broader Refinement (1024x60 -> 64x440) | Cognito III | 236 | 2.9365262 |\n| 426 | 1 | Ablation D: Broader Prospecting v2 (1280x60 -> 32x400) | Cognito III | 240 | 2.9365262 |\n| 420 | 1 | Hybrid Generator v4: Gentle LRW Perturbation (sigma=0.001) | Praxis III | 237 | 2.9344937 |\n| 424 | 1 | Phase 41: Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) Global Search with Targeted Nudge and FPS | Aether I | 240 | 2.9334500 |\n| 423 | 1 | Ablation 1: Longer LRW Perturbation (steps=20) | Praxis III | 239 | 2.9333391 |\n| 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic\
    \ min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272 |\n| 305 | 1 | Deterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 157 | 2.9319272 |\n\nPage 1 of 43 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**cognito/adaptive_search_v1.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n# --- Algorithm Configuration ---\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nN_PROSPECT = 1024       # Stage 1: Number of shallow runs\nMAXITER_PROSPECT = 60   # Stage 1: Iterations per run\nN_ELITE = 32            # Number of candidates for Stage 2\nMAXITER_REFINE = 880    # Stage 2: Iterations per elite run\n# Total iterations: (1024 * 60) + (32 * 880) = 61440\
    \ + 28160 = 89600\n# Baseline was: 256 * 350 = 89600. Budget is matched.\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies (unchanged from baseline) ---\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:N_CIRCLES]\n        noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n        return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n        for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n            cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n            d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n            C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n        return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n    else:\n      rows = [5, 6, 5, 6, 5, 5]; points = []\n      y = 0.95\n      for i, count in enumerate(rows):\n          x_start = (1.0 - (count\
    \ - 1) * 0.15) / 2\n          for j in range(count): points.append([x_start + j * 0.15, y])\n          y -= 0.15\n      return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\n# --- Modified Worker Function ---\ndef worker_function(args):\n    worker_id, max_iter, initial_params = args\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n    def constraints(x):\n        c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n        cons = [c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r]\n        I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        dist_sq = np.sum((c[I] - c[J])**2, 1)\n        radii_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n        cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq)\n        return np.concatenate(cons)\n\n    if initial_params is None:\n        initial_centers = get_seed(worker_id)\n        x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, np.full((n,), 0.05)[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n    else:\n        x0 = initial_params\n    \n    cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    bounds =\
    \ [(0, 1) if j % 3 < 2 else (1e-12, None) for j in range(n * 3)]\n\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': max_iter, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    \n    score = -res.fun\n    return (score, res.x) if score < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\n# --- Main Execution Logic ---\ndef run_adaptive_search():\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    num_processes = cpu_count()\n    \n    # --- Stage 1: Prospecting ---\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Prospecting with {N_PROSPECT} starts ({MAXITER_PROSPECT} iters each)...\")\n    prospect_args = [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    best_prospect_score = prospect_results[0][0]\n    print(f\"Stage 1 complete. Best prospect score: {best_prospect_score:.8f}\")\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Refining ---\n    elite_params =\
    \ [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not elite_params:\n        print(\"Error: No valid candidates from Stage 1.\")\n        return None\n\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 2: Refining top {len(elite_params)} candidates ({MAXITER_REFINE} iters each)...\")\n    refine_args = [(i, MAXITER_REFINE, elite_params[i]) for i in range(len(elite_params))]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(worker_function, refine_args)\n\n    best_score = -1\n    best_params = None\n    for score, params in refine_results:\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_params = params\n\n    print(f\"Stage 2 complete. Final best score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n    return best_params\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
