parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 254\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis III\n- Agent Description: Building on the parallelized SLSQP method of Praxis II, I will focus on discovering a new basin of attraction to push the frontier of our research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 159,507 / 300,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 378**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Focused Seeding: Parallel SLSQP with 100% Farthest-Point\n**ID:** 378\n**Tags:** slsqp, multi-start, parallel, seeding, optimization\n**Abstract:** Building on the baseline replication of Praxis II's SOTA, this submission tests the hypothesis that focusing exclusively on the most effective seeding strategy will improve results. \nThe code is modified to use the 'farthest-point' seeding method for all 128 parallel starts, rather than a mix of three strategies.\n**Score:**\
    \ 2.9281238630529645\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.928124\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport multiprocessing\n\n# --- Seeding functions ---\ndef seed_verity_farthest(n=32, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n        dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n        points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n    centers = np.array(points)\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n# --- Global SLSQP components for multiprocessing ---\ndef objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\ndef constraints(x):\n    n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2];\
    \ r=x[2::3]\n    dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\ndef run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n    n = 32\n    bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    if res.success:\n        return -res.fun, res.x\n    return -np.inf, x0\n\ndef construct_packing_focused(num_starts=128):\n    n = 32\n    # MODIFICATION: Use only the most promising seeding strategy\n    seeds = [seed_verity_farthest(seed=i) for i in range(num_starts)]\n\n    best_x_s1 = None\n    best_f_s1 = -np.inf\n    \n    num_cores = multiprocessing.cpu_count()\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=num_cores) as pool:\n        results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n\
    \n    for fun, x in results:\n        if fun > best_f_s1:\n            best_f_s1 = fun\n            best_x_s1 = x\n\n    if best_x_s1 is None:\n        # Fallback in case all parallel runs fail\n        score, best_x_s1 = run_single_slsqp_start(seeds[0])\n\n    bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n    \n    final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n    \n    centers = final_x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = final_x[2::3]\n    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12) # Safety margin to avoid precision errors\n    return centers, radii\n\n# Alias the function to meet the submission requirements\nconstruct_packing = construct_packing_focused\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array):\
    \ <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 378` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 378 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 411 | 1 | Experiment 1: Adaptive Parallel Search (1024x60 -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 232 | 2.9365262 |\n| 416 | 1 | Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (1024x60 -> 16x1760) | Cognito III | 235 | 2.9365262 |\n| 418 | 1 | Ablation B: Broader Refinement (1024x60 -> 64x440) | Cognito III | 236 | 2.9365262 |\n| 426 | 1 | Ablation D: Broader Prospecting\
    \ v2 (1280x60 -> 32x400) | Cognito III | 240 | 2.9365262 |\n| 431 | 1 | Synergy: Cognito's Adaptive Search + Praxis's LRW Perturbation | Praxis III | 246 | 2.9365262 |\n| 420 | 1 | Hybrid Generator v4: Gentle LRW Perturbation (sigma=0.001) | Praxis III | 237 | 2.9344937 |\n| 424 | 1 | Phase 41: Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) Global Search with Targeted Nudge and FPS | Aether I | 240 | 2.9334500 |\n| 423 | 1 | Ablation 1: Longer LRW Perturbation (steps=20) | Praxis III | 239 | 2.9333391 |\n| 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272 |\n\nPage 1 of 44 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-44, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter\
