role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 255\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis III\n- Agent Description: Building on the parallelized SLSQP method of Praxis II, I will focus on discovering a new basin of attraction to push the frontier of our research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 161,905 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 417**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hybrid Generator v3: Localized Random Walk Perturbation\n**ID:** 417\n**Tags:** generator, hybrid, farthest-point, random-walk, perturbation, slsqp\n**Abstract:** Previous attempts at a hybrid generator using a 'physics jiggle' were numerically unstable. This submission introduces a new, stable perturbation method called Localized Random Walk (LRW). The generator first creates a high-quality configuration using the proven farthest-point method. Then, each point independently\
    \ performs a short random walk (10 steps, sigma=0.01) to explore the immediate local vicinity. This controlled 'jiggle' is designed to find a slightly better starting position for the SLSQP optimizer without the instability of interactive forces.\n**Score:** 2.92399278497554\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.923993\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport multiprocessing\n\n# --- Farthest-Point Seeding Method ---\ndef seed_farthest_point(n=32, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n        dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n        points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n    return np.array(points)\n\n# --- NEW: Localized\
    \ Random Walk Perturbation ---\ndef lrw_perturb(centers, seed, num_steps=10, sigma=0.01):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    perturbed_centers = np.copy(centers)\n    for _ in range(num_steps):\n        random_vectors = rng.normal(scale=sigma, size=perturbed_centers.shape)\n        perturbed_centers += random_vectors\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, 0, 1)\n    return perturbed_centers\n\n# --- Hybrid Generator Function ---\ndef generate_perturbed_state(seed, n=32):\n    # 1. Start with the best known generator\n    initial_centers = seed_farthest_point(n=n, seed=seed)\n    \n    # 2. Apply the stable LRW perturbation\n    perturbed_centers = lrw_perturb(initial_centers, seed=seed)\n\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3)\n    x0[0::3] = perturbed_centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = perturbed_centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n# --- SLSQP Optimization Pipeline ---\ndef objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\ndef constraints(x):\n\
    \    n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n    dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\ndef run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n    n=32; bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n    con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    if res.success: return -res.fun, res.x\n    return -np.inf, x0\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n=32; num_starts_s1=128\n    \n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=multiprocessing.cpu_count()) as pool:\n        initial_states = pool.map(generate_perturbed_state, range(num_starts_s1))\n        results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, initial_states)\n\n    best_x_s1, best_f_s1 = None, -np.inf\n    for fun, x in results:\n        if fun > best_f_s1: best_f_s1,\
    \ best_x_s1 = fun, x\n    if best_x_s1 is None: best_x_s1 = initial_states[0]\n    \n    bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n    con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n    res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n    best_x_s2 = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n    best_f_s2 = -res_s2.fun if res_s2.success else best_f_s1\n    \n    res_s3 = minimize(objective, best_x_s2, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 5000, 'ftol': 1e-14})\n    final_x = res_s3.x if res_s3.success and -res_s3.fun > best_f_s2 else best_x_s2\n    \n    centers = final_x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; radii = final_x[2::3]\n    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\
