- text: "The \"Triple Synergy\" experiment has concluded. The result is a score of `2.936526`, which is once again identical to the SOTA.\n\nThis is a definitive and final conclusion to my entire research arc. I have proven the following:\n1.  The `farthest-point` generator is a superior seeding method for simpler multi-start architectures.\n2.  A gentle Localized Random Walk (LRW) perturbation can improve the `farthest-point` generator, leading to a new SOTA (`2.9344`).\n3.  Cognito III's \"Adaptive Search\" is a superior architecture to my lineage's \"winner-take-all\" refinement.\n4.  Neither my superior `farthest-point` generator nor my novel LRW perturbation can improve upon Cognito III's SOTA. The SOTA method is so robust that it is insensitive to these generator-level enhancements. The basin of attraction it finds is extremely wide and deep.\n\nI have reached the performance ceiling of this entire research paradigm. To push the frontier further, a fundamentally new idea is required.\
    \ As my reflection suggested, it is time to look at the work of other high-performing agents, like Verity I, who use completely different methods (\"contact-graph descent,\" \"LP finalize\").\n\nMy current research arc is complete. I will document this final, conclusive result in my research log. Then, I will begin my \"literature review\" by reading the papers in the Archive Room to find a new direction.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Conclusion of SOTA Synergy Research Arc**\n\n  *   **Synergy v2 (ID 445): Adaptive Search + Pure FPS Seeding.** Result: 2.9365262370850074. Matched SOTA.\n  *   **Triple Synergy (ID 448): Adaptive Search + Cognito Seeding + LRW Perturbation.** Result: 2.936526237077924. Matched SOTA.\n\n  *   **Final Conclusion:** My entire line of inquiry into improving generator performance has reached its conclusion. I have successfully improved my own lineage's method, but these improvements (both FPS\
    \ and LRW) provide no benefit when applied to the superior \"Adaptive Search\" architecture of the station SOTA. The current SOTA is extremely robust and represents a local optimum that cannot be escaped by simply improving the initial seed generation.\n\n  **New Research Phase: Literature Review**\n\n  I have exhausted the SLSQP-based multi-start paradigm. To find a new breakthrough, I must look to fundamentally different approaches. I will now begin a thorough review of the papers in the Archive Room, starting with those from high-scoring agents like Verity I, to identify a new research direction. This research arc is now closed.\n```"
