tick: 273
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully generated and saved my SOTA artifact. The center coordinates are now available in my logs and stored in `praxis/sota_artifact_420.npz`. I can now proceed with my plan to implement and test the LP radii solver.\n\nI have also received a token budget warning. I am over 75% usage. This adds urgency to my work. I must make my next experiments count. My plan to unit test the LP solver is even more critical now, as it is a low-cost way to verify my understanding before attempting a more complex, token-intensive experiment.\n\nI will now submit the LP solver test. The code will be simple: load the centers from my artifact, formulate the linear program for the radii, solve it, and return the result. This will validate my LP formulation, which is the foundational step for my new research direction.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Unit Test: Exact LP Radii Solver on Praxis SOTA Artifact\"\ntags: \"lp, linear programming, verity replication, unit test,\
    \ artifact\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first step in replicating Verity I's LP-guided methodology. This submission serves as a unit test to validate the core component: an exact Linear Program (LP) solver for circle radii, given a fixed set of centers. The script loads the center coordinates from my SOTA artifact (ID 420, score 2.93449), formulates the LP to maximize the sum of radii subject to non-overlap and boundary constraints, and solves it using SciPy's 'highs' solver. The goal is to verify the LP formulation is correct.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import sys\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n      \n      # Load the centers from my SOTA artifact\n      try:\n          artifact = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_420.npz')\n          centers = artifact['centers']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          # Fallback if the artifact is not found\n          print(\"Artifact not found, using a dummy\
    \ configuration.\")\n          centers = np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n\n      if centers.shape != (N_CIRCLES, 2):\n          raise ValueError(\"Loaded centers have incorrect shape.\")\n\n      # --- LP Formulation for Radii ---\n      # Objective: Maximize sum(radii), which is equivalent to minimizing -sum(radii)\n      c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n      \n      # Constraints:\n      # A_ub @ radii <= b_ub\n      \n      # 1. Boundary constraints: c_x - r >= 0, c_x + r <= 1, etc.\n      # Rewritten as: r <= c_x, r <= 1 - c_x, r <= c_y, r <= 1 - c_y\n      A_boundary = []\n      b_boundary = []\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          cx, cy = centers[i]\n          # r_i <= cx\n          row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_boundary.append(row); b_boundary.append(cx)\n          # r_i <= 1 - cx\n          row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_boundary.append(row); b_boundary.append(1 - cx)\n          # r_i <= cy\n          row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_boundary.append(row);\
    \ b_boundary.append(cy)\n          # r_i <= 1 - cy\n          row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_boundary.append(row); b_boundary.append(1 - cy)\n          \n      # 2. Pairwise non-overlap constraints: r_i + r_j <= distance(c_i, c_j)\n      A_pairwise = []\n      b_pairwise = []\n      indices = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n      for i, j in zip(*indices):\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n          row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES)\n          row[i] = 1\n          row[j] = 1\n          A_pairwise.append(row)\n          b_pairwise.append(dist)\n\n      A_ub = np.vstack([A_boundary, A_pairwise])\n      b_ub = np.hstack([b_boundary, b_pairwise])\n      \n      # Radii must be positive (lower bound)\n      bounds = (0, None)\n\n      # Solve the LP using the HiGHS solver\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n\n      if res.success:\n          radii = res.x\n          # Apply a small safety shrink, as per Verity I's papers\n\
    \          return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n      else:\n          # Fallback if solver fails\n          print(\"LP solver failed. Returning fallback.\")\n          return centers, np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.01)\n```"
