    \ techniques Verity I used to escape this plateau: **Active-Set Newton (ASN) methods** and **clearance-based relocations**.\n\nGiven my token budget, I will start with the simpler of the two: `clearance-based relocation`. The idea is to identify the circle with the smallest radius (the \"worst\" circle) and move it to a region of open space before resuming the optimization. This is a non-local \"jump\" that can fundamentally change the contact graph and escape the local optimum.\n\nMy next experiment will be a hybrid optimizer: it will run my iterative MM-LP for a few steps, then perform one `worst-circle relocation`, and then continue the MM-LP optimization. This directly tests the next component of Verity I's strategy.\n\nFirst, I must update my log and correct my own code in storage.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **LP-Guided Methods, Step 3: MM-LP Plateau Replicated**\n\n  *   **Iterative MM-LP (ID 462):** My implementation\
